# COMMITTED ON PURPOSE — no secrets in this file. See README "Env".
#
# Development must never reach the hosted ledger, so this mode file pins
# `bun dev` / `next dev` to the local SQLite database. Next.js and Bun both load
# `.env.<mode>` ABOVE `.env` and BELOW `.env.local` / `.env.<mode>.local`, and
# they carry the same file into a fresh clone. Net effect:
#   - a `libsql://` URL sitting in `.env` cannot drag development onto
#     production, and
#   - the behaviour is still overridable on purpose, per machine, via
#     `.env.local`, `.env.development.local`, or a shell export (highest wins).
DATABASE_URL="file:./ledger.db"
